as-module-licenses-expire\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>Sangoma is rolling out further changes to commercial module versioning, dependency handling, and security on FreePBX and PBXact. If your team uses Talk Mobile, the Desktop Client, or the Web Phone, here\\u2019s the plain-English version of what\\u2019s changing \\u2014 and what to check before it catches you off guard. Who this affects\\u00a0 This\\u00a0one\\u2019s\\u00a0for you if\\u00a0you\\u2019re\\u00a0running [\\u2026]<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/softphone-access-is-changing-as-module-licenses-expire\\/\\\">Softphone access is changing as module licenses expire<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Avoid walking the plank with expired modules\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/avoid-walking-the-plank-with-expired-modules\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>With the recent brisk pace of FreePBX security improvements, we are seeing increased reports in our community forums and elsewhere from users who are encountering issues when modules won\'t upgrade to the latest version or stop working in subtle ways because of out-of-date third-party pseudo-mirrors.<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/avoid-walking-the-plank-with-expired-modules\\/\\\">Avoid walking the plank with expired modules<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Tango is now old enough to get a license to operate a motor vehicle\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/tango-is-now-old-enough-to-get-a-license-to-operate-a-motor-vehicle\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>Ring, ring, beep, beep! Tango the FreePBX frog is turning 17, hopping in the van and driving West to AstriCon 2026 for 4 FreePBX talks \\ud83d\\udc38\\ud83d\\ude90\\ud83e\\udd20\\ud83c\\udf34 Tango on the road to AstriCon. Tango celebrates bowl games en route This frog is having some serious fun ahead of the AstriCon conference in California from March 5-6, [\\u2026]<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/tango-is-now-old-enough-to-get-a-license-to-operate-a-motor-vehicle\\/\\\">Tango is now old enough to get a license to operate a motor vehicle<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"New SAML module for improved login security\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/saml-for-improved-login-security\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>This new SAML module makes it easier than ever to integrate your FreePBX and PBXact systems with your existing single sign-on solutions, enhancing security and simplifying access for your team.<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/saml-for-improved-login-security\\/\\\">New SAML module for improved login security<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Finally! A Better Way to Visualize Dial Plans\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/finally-a-better-way-to-visualize-dial-plans\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>Whether you\\u2019re configuring, troubleshooting, or simply exploring, Dial Plan Vizualizer helps you see the invisible\\u2014and that makes all the difference.<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/finally-a-better-way-to-visualize-dial-plans\\/\\\">Finally! A Better Way to Visualize Dial Plans<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"If Speech-To-Text backwards is Text-To-Speech, then SCRIBE is EBIRCS\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/if-speech-to-text-backwards-is-text-to-speech-then-scribe-is-ebircs\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>It\\u2019s been almost a year since we launched Scribe for FreePBX and PBXact, bringing powerful AI transcription to your fingertips. But Scribe is more than just transcription\\u2014it\\u2019s a rapidly evolving service designed to unlock actionable insights from every call and voicemail message.\\u00a0<\\/p>\\n<p>Today, we\'re excited to introduce a host of new features that make Scribe an even more indispensable tool for your business.<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/if-speech-to-text-backwards-is-text-to-speech-then-scribe-is-ebircs\\/\\\">If Speech-To-Text backwards is Text-To-Speech, then SCRIBE is EBIRCS<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Watch what we do with security fixes \\ud83d\\udc40\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/watch-what-we-do-with-security-fixes-%F0%9F%91%80\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>This article discusses meta-issues surrounding security fixes in FreePBX, investigates vulnerability scoring tools, and offers some ideas for improvements. System Administrators should walk away with a better understanding of terms like CVE, CWE, CVSS (including the differences between Base and other metrics), and EPSS.<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/watch-what-we-do-with-security-fixes-%F0%9F%91%80\\/\\\">Watch what we do with security fixes \\ud83d\\udc40<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"Sangoma\\u2019s Browser-Based Soft Phone \\u2013 Seamless Communication, Zero Installation\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/sangomas-browser-based-soft-phone-seamless-communication-zero-installation\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>The Sangoma Phone Browser-Based Client provides a powerful, feature-rich softphone experience\\u2014accessible directly from your web browser, with no software installation required. It delivers the same robust communication features as the Sangoma Phone desktop application, ensuring a consistent user experience across platforms. Designed for today\\u2019s flexible work environments, the browser-based client integrates effortlessly with Sangoma\\u2019s Asterisk-based [\\u2026]<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/sangomas-browser-based-soft-phone-seamless-communication-zero-installation\\/\\\">Sangoma\\u2019s Browser-Based Soft Phone \\u2013 Seamless Communication, Zero Installation<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"On a Roll: Sangoma Desktop Client Gains More Security and Launches Extra Features\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/on-a-roll-sangoma-desktop-client-gains-more-security-and-launches-extra-features\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>We\\u2019re pleased to share that new features have been added to the Sangoma Desktop Client. These updates aim to improve the user experience and make the soft client more secure, efficient and user-friendly. Multi-Factor Authentication Support Starting from version 4.0.6, the Sangoma Desktop Client (SDC) now supports Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA).\\u00a0The latest features introduced in SDC, [\\u2026]<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/on-a-roll-sangoma-desktop-client-gains-more-security-and-launches-extra-features\\/\\\">On a Roll: Sangoma Desktop Client Gains More Security and Launches Extra Features<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"},{\"title\":\"FreePBX World Summit 2025 \\u2013 Call For Speakers\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/freepbx-world-summit-2025-call-for-speakers\\/\",\"content\":\"<p>Attending The Linux Foundation\\u2019s Open Source Summit? Join us in Denver, Colorado, on the morning of June 26, 2025! \\u00a0 FreePBX World Summit 2025, proudly sponsored by Sangoma, brings together users and contributors of FreePBX \\u2013 the world\\u2019s most popular open source GUI for the Asterisk telephony toolkit. Over twenty years in the making, FreePBX [\\u2026]<\\/p>\\n<p>The post <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/freepbx-world-summit-2025-call-for-speakers\\/\\\">FreePBX World Summit 2025 \\u2013 Call For Speakers<\\/a> appeared first on <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/www.freepbx.org\\/\\\">FreePBX - Let Freedom Ring<\\/a>.<\\/p>\"}]}'),('1706f065-e858-46ea-9d10-41cb6c51f95f','json-arr','{\"psi.@attributes.xmlns:tns\":\"http:\\/\\/phpsysinfo.sourceforge.net\\/\",\"psi.@attributes.xmlns:xsi\":\"http:\\/\\/www.w3.org\\/2001\\/XMLSchema-instance\",\"psi.@attributes.xsi:schemaLocation\":\"http:\\/\\/phpsysinfo.sourceforge.net\\/ phpsysinfo3.xsd\",\"psi.Generation.@attributes.version\":\"3.1.11\",\"psi.Options.@attributes.tempFormat\":\"c\",\"psi.Options.@attributes.byteFormat\":\"auto_binary\",\"psi.Options.@attributes.showPickListTemplate\":\"true\",\"psi.Options.@attributes.showPickListLang\":\"true\",\"psi.UsedPlugins.Plugin.0.@attributes.name\":\"mdstatus\",\"psi.UsedPlugins.Plugin.1.@attributes.name\":\"smart\",\"psi.UsedPlugins.Plugin.2.@attributes.name\":\"ipmiinfo\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.Hostname\":\"pbx1.rusagroeco.ru\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.IPAddr\":\"127.0.1.1\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.Kernel\":\"5.10.0-8-amd64 (SMP) x86_64\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.Distro\":\"Debian GNU\\/Linux 11 (bullseye)\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.Distroicon\":\"Debian.png\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.LoadAvg\":\"0.42 0.25 0.19\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.SysLang\":\"English United States (en_US)\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.CodePage\":\"UTF-8\",\"psi.Vitals.@attributes.OS\":\"Linux\",\"psi.Network.NetDevice.0.@attributes.Name\":\"lo\",\"psi.Network.NetDevice.1.@attributes.Name\":\"eth0\",\"psi.Hardware.PCI.Device.0.@attributes.Name\":\"Host bridge: Intel Corporation 440BX\\/ZX\\/DX - 82443BX\\/ZX\\/DX Host bridge\",\"psi.Hardware.PCI.Device.1.@attributes.Name\":\"ISA bridge: Intel Corporation 82371AB\\/EB\\/MB PIIX4 ISA\",\"psi.Hardware.PCI.Device.2.@attributes.Name\":\"IDE interface: Intel Corporation 82371AB\\/EB\\/MB PIIX4 ID